  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with and find humor in gendered stereotypes, particularly those that hypersexualize men based on their appearance (e.g., manbun hairstyle). The meme appeals to an audience that understands and engages with internet humor rooted in objectification and sexualized tropes, often found in online communities that share memes with misogynous undertones. The audience likely includes people who recognize the manbun as a cultural signifier of masculinity or sexual availability and who find the juxtaposition of the image with the hypersexualized text amusing, even if it is offensive to others. The meme’s humor is derived from reinforcing a stereotype that reduces a man’s identity to a sexualized trait, which is a common trope in certain online spaces that prioritize shock value or exaggerated humor over sensitivity.",
